hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24284","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Khalid, meaning al-Hadhdha', from Abu Bishr al-Anbari, from Ibn al-Talib, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): That a man freed a share of his from a slave, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not make him liable. Ghundar said thus: Ibn al-Thalib, but it is: Ibn al-Talib, and Shu'bah had something in his tongue, meaning a lisp, and perhaps Ghundar did not understand from him."
